# Table Actions Column — Single Format (all modules)

**Rule:** Every list/table **Actions** column uses the **same** control style across the whole OMS. Do not invent per-screen Action UIs (text labels, More menus, mixed styles).

Reference screens that already follow this: Tasks list, Projects list, Requirements list, Employees patterns.

## Canonical format (required)

Icon-only Bootstrap outline buttons inside `btn-group btn-group-sm`:

```php
<td class="text-end text-nowrap">
  <div class="btn-group btn-group-sm" role="group" aria-label="Actions">
    <a href="..." class="btn btn-outline-secondary" title="View"><i class="bi bi-eye"></i></a>
    <a href="..." class="btn btn-outline-primary" title="Edit"><i class="bi bi-pencil"></i></a>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-danger" title="Delete" ...>
      <i class="bi bi-trash"></i>
    </button>
  </div>
</td>
```

## Required details

| Item | Standard |
|------|----------|
| Wrapper | `btn-group btn-group-sm` + `role="group"` |
| Cell | `text-end text-nowrap` |
| Control | Icon **only** — no label text like "View" / "Edit" / "Delete" next to the icon |
| Accessibility | `title="..."` and/or `aria-label="..."` on every control |
| Icons | Bootstrap Icons only (`bi bi-*`) |
| Header | Actions column header uses `class="text-end"` (or `text-end text-nowrap`) |

## Color map (keep consistent)

| Action | Class | Icon |
|--------|-------|------|
| View / open | `btn-outline-secondary` | `bi-eye` |
| Edit | `btn-outline-primary` | `bi-pencil` |
| Approve / success | `btn-outline-success` | `bi-check-lg` |
| Reject / warning soft | `btn-outline-warning` | `bi-x-lg` (or module-specific) |
| Delete / danger | `btn-outline-danger` | `bi-trash` |
| Download / export | `btn-outline-secondary` | `bi-download` |
| Extra tools | `btn-outline-secondary` | matching `bi-*` |

## Forbidden (do not introduce)

- Text buttons in Actions: `View`, `Edit`, `Delete` labels beside icons
- **More / ⋮ dropdown menus** inside the Actions column (duplicates View/Edit and clips under `overflow: auto` / sticky table wrappers)
- Mixing styles on the same page (one row icon-only, another full text button)
- Raw icons without `btn` classes
- `d-flex gap-1` loose buttons when `btn-group` fits (prefer `btn-group`)
- Different icon sets (Font Awesome, emoji) in Actions columns
- Large `btn` (non-sm) in dense tables
- Centering Actions when the project standard is `text-end` (right-aligned)

## Overflow / clipping note

List tables often use `overflow: auto` or sticky headers. **Dropdowns inside Actions will clip or overlap rows.** Prefer direct icon buttons + confirm modal/dialog for Delete — never rely on a row dropdown for primary actions.

## Forms / page headers (exception)

Toolbar and page-header primary actions **may** use text + icon (e.g. `btn btn-primary btn-sm` + "Add Client"). That exception is **only** outside the table Actions column.

## When editing existing screens

If you touch a table Actions column that uses text buttons, More menus, or mixed styles, **normalize it** to this icon `btn-group` format in the same change (same module file only — do not drive-by other modules unless asked).
